# Expectation record for 02_constant_expressions/006_conditional_and_comma_folding.c
#
# Reproduce one cell by hand with no harness: render the three command templates
# below, substituting the target triple, the optimization level, the source path,
# the output path, and the target's runner (empty on the natively executing target).

program            = 006_conditional_and_comma_folding
area               = 02_constant_expressions
description        = Folding through the conditional and comma operators, with side-effecting comma operands and volatile-operand runtime twins
targets            = x86_64, i686, aarch64, riscv64
opt_levels         = -O0, -O1, -O2
shared_flags       = -static
bcc_command        = $BCC --target <triple> <opt> -static <src> -o <out>
ref_command        = $REF_CC_<TRIPLE> <opt> -static <src> -o <out>
run_command        = <runner> <out>
expect_exit        = 0
oracle_a           = enabled
oracle_b           = enabled
oracle_c           = enabled
ub_notes           <<END
This program contains no undefined behaviour and depends on no unspecified behaviour, which is the
precondition that makes both differential oracles sound rather than a stylistic preference:
undefined behaviour would license either compiler to do anything at all, so a divergence between
them would prove nothing about either one. Sequencing is unusually worth spelling out here, because
sequencing is also the subject under test -- the argument below rests on the very two operators the
program exists to exercise.
THE TWO OPERATORS UNDER TEST ARE THE TWO THAT SUPPLY THE SEQUENCE POINTS THIS ARGUMENT RESTS ON. The
comma operator sequences every side effect of its left operand before its right operand is evaluated
(C11 6.5.17p2), and the conditional operator evaluates exactly one of its second and third operands,
after its controlling expression and after the sequence point between them (C11 6.5.15p4). The
ordering of every side effect printed here is therefore fixed by the standard rather than left
unspecified, so nothing in this program depends on unspecified evaluation order, which requirement 1
forbids outright.
NO OBJECT IS MODIFIED TWICE BETWEEN TWO SEQUENCE POINTS. Every modification of a counter or an
accumulator is separated from the next by a comma operator's sequence point or by a statement
boundary. There is no expression of the form v = v++, no v++ + v++, and -- the case that matters most
for this program -- no chain that combines a comma-sequenced modification of an object with a second
modification of that same object elsewhere in the same full expression. The two four-step chains are
the concrete instance: plain_chain is modified twice and vchain is modified twice, each time as the
left operand of a comma whose sequence point separates it from the next step, and neither object is
touched anywhere else in the full expression that contains it. The same holds for the pair v7 and v6,
which are assigned in the two left operands and only read in the right operand, after both sequence
points; and for the volatile counter ticks, which is incremented at most once per full expression.
NO CALL RECEIVES MORE THAN ONE ARGUMENT WITH A SIDE EFFECT. The order in which a call's arguments are
evaluated is unspecified (C11 6.5.2.2p10), so two side-effecting arguments would make the printed
order unspecified as well, and requirement 1 forbids depending on it. Where a printed line needs both
a value produced by a side-effecting expression and a counter read afterwards, the side effect is
sequenced in a statement of its own first and the counter is snapshotted into a plain local --
hits_then_seen, hits_else_seen, ticks_seen -- before the call. The one call that does receive a
side-effecting argument, identity((ticks = ticks + 1, 6 * 7)) and its volatile twin, takes exactly
one argument, so there is no second argument for its evaluation to be ordered against.
EVERY COMMA EXPRESSION'S LEFT OPERAND PERFORMS A REAL SIDE EFFECT, BY DESIGN. A comma expression
whose left operand computes a value nobody uses is what -Wunused-value exists to diagnose, and -Wall
enables it while -Werror makes it fatal, so the default gate rejects that shape outright. Area 02
sanctions no gate deviation, so the constraint is met by writing the expressions differently -- every
left operand here is an assignment to volatile or plain storage, a counter increment, or a for-clause
-- and never by weakening the gate, which would trade a real check for a silence.
The restriction improves the program rather than constraining it: a side-effecting left operand is
exactly what makes the sequence point observable, and observable sequencing is the interesting
property of the comma operator.
ARM SUPPRESSION IS OBSERVED THROUGH VOLATILE COUNTERS, WHICH IS THE ONLY WAY AN ABSENCE CAN BE
ASSERTED. The conditional operator's guarantee is partly negative -- the unselected arm is not
evaluated -- and an assertion that a side effect did not happen is meaningful only if the
implementation is obliged to honour the observation. The counters then_hits, else_hits and ticks are
therefore volatile: a volatile access is part of the program's observable behaviour, so no
optimization may elide the evidence, whereas a plain counter could legally be folded away and the
absence would then prove nothing. Each printed counter line names both arms, and the unselected arm's
step is 100 rather than 1, so an arm evaluated in error is unmistakable in the output instead of
merely off by one.
THE REST OF THE RULEBOOK IS SATISFIED BY CONSTRUCTION. No signed arithmetic can overflow: every int
result printed is 42 or smaller except the deliberate counter value 100 and the loop sum 28, and the
wide arithmetic is performed in long long built from LL-suffixed literals, whose largest product is
6LL * 1000000000LL == 6000000000 -- orders of magnitude inside the 64-bit minimum range the standard
guarantees for long long, on every target including the 32-bit one. The one unsigned result, printed
as 4294967295, is the modular reduction of 0u - 1u, which C11 6.2.5p9 defines for every value and
which is therefore not undefined at all rather than an overflow that happens to be survivable. No
shift of any kind occurs anywhere in the file. There is no aliasing violation and no pointer
question to answer, because the only pointer in the program is the string literal passed to printf:
no object's address is taken, no one-past-the-end pointer is formed at all -- let alone dereferenced
-- no object representation is inspected, no padding byte is observed, and nothing depends on the
relative addresses of unrelated objects. No storage is read uninitialized: every object is
initialized in its own declaration or assigned before its first read, and the one array,
folded_bound_probe, has static storage duration -- so its contents are fully determined -- and is
only ever measured with sizeof, never read. sizeof does not evaluate its operand (C11 6.5.3.4p2), so
the volatile objects that appear inside a sizeof are not accessed there and the number of volatile
accesses stays exactly what the source shows.
NO HEADER IS NAMED ANYWHERE and the single libc prototype the program needs, printf, is declared by
hand as `int printf(const char *, ...);` -- the corpus-wide rule stated in
tests/conformance/README.md, whose two sanctioned exceptions are area 07's stdarg.h and area 12's
bundled-header probe, neither of which applies here. In fact the file contains no preprocessing
directive of any kind.
NOTHING IN THIS FILE IS A GCC EXTENSION, AND IN PARTICULAR THERE IS NO STATEMENT EXPRESSION. The
sequence `({` does not occur anywhere in the program -- checked mechanically, by stripping comments
and string literals and finding none -- and neither does typeof, __typeof__, any __-prefixed
identifier, or _Generic. A statement expression is a tempting near-neighbour of this subject matter,
since it too produces a value from a sequence of side effects, but it belongs to area
08_gcc_extensions, which is the only area permitted to drop -pedantic for exactly that reason.
Because this program stays inside the standard language, area 02 needs neither an include exception
nor a gate deviation, and neither is taken.
THIS RECORD DECLARES NO WARNING-GATE DEVIATION: no ub_audit_flags key appears above, so the program
is audited under the suite's full default gate. That is a measured claim, not an intention. It is
clean -- zero diagnostics, empty stderr -- under -Wall -Wextra -pedantic -Wconversion
-Wsign-conversion -Wshadow -Werror in the single native compile-only invocation the suite's warning
gate makes; and it builds and then runs clean, with an empty stderr and exit status 0, under the
sanitizer gate -fsanitize=undefined,address -fno-sanitize-recover=all. Both gates are
reference-compiler-only and are never applied to bcc -- the technical specification lists sanitizers
among its explicit exclusions (docs/technical-specifications.md line 713, section 0.6.2) -- so
requirement 3's shared-flag discipline is untouched by either of them.
OUTPUT IS FULLY DETERMINISTIC: no address, no timestamp, no randomness, no locale-dependent
formatting, literal loop bounds throughout, and every value printed with %d or %lld matched exactly
to its argument's type -- those two conversions are the only ones the file uses. main returns 0,
inside the 0-125 range the suite requires so that no exit status is truncated by the operating
system. Every input is a literal in this file, so every cell is reproducible from this source and
this record alone.
END
impl_defined_notes <<END
THIS RECORD NARROWS NOTHING. All four targets are declared, all three optimization levels are swept,
all three oracles are enabled, and no ub_audit_flags key appears. These notes therefore record the
normalizations that make the full four-way comparison SOUND, rather than excusing a comparison that
was not made -- there is no exclusion here to explain.
THE CONDITIONAL OPERATOR'S RESULT TYPE IS DELIBERATELY OBSERVED, AND EVERY COMMON TYPE IT SELECTS IS
THE SAME ON ALL FOUR TARGETS. Three lines print (int)sizeof applied to a conditional expression, which
reports the width of the common type its two arms select: int against int gives 4, int against long
long gives 8, and unsigned int against unsigned int gives 4. Those widths are implementation-defined
in principle, because C11 fixes only minimum ranges for the integer types, so they were measured
rather than assumed. The program was built and executed on all four supported targets at -O0, -O1 and
-O2 -- twelve configurations -- and every one printed the same 67 lines byte-identically, 1826 bytes
each, including fold_result_size_int=4, fold_result_size_llong=8 and fold_result_size_uint=4 together
with their runtime twins. The arms of every conditional are chosen so the common type cannot vary by
target: the pairs are int/int, int/long long and unsigned int/unsigned int, never a pair whose ranking
depends on how wide long or a pointer happens to be. Because the widths agree on all four targets and
the measured values agree, cross-backend comparison of this program is sound and oracle (b) remains
enabled for it.
EVERY CONVERSION THAT CHANGES A WIDTH OR A SIGNEDNESS IS WRITTEN AS AN EXPLICIT CAST. The size lines
cast the size_t result of sizeof to int; the wrapped unsigned value is cast to long long before being
printed with %lld; and the wide product casts its int operand to long long. Nothing is narrowed or
re-signed implicitly, which is also why -Wconversion and -Wsign-conversion can stay in the audit gate
for this program rather than being dropped from it: an implicit conversion here would be a defect in
the test, not a diagnostic to suppress.
THE TWO MEASURED DIFFERENCES BETWEEN THE SUPPORTED TARGETS CANNOT REACH THIS PROGRAM BY CONSTRUCTION.
Plain char is never used as a value type and no character value is formed or printed -- the only char
in the file is the const char * of the printf prototype -- so the plain-char signedness difference,
signed on x86_64 and i686 and unsigned on aarch64 and riscv64, is unreachable here. Plain long is
never declared and never printed either, verified mechanically by collapsing every `long long` and
finding no bare `long` left, so the i686 difference in sizeof(long) and sizeof(void *) -- 4 bytes
there against 8 on the other three, recorded in the target table at docs/technical-specifications.md
lines 457-462 -- is unreachable as well. Every wide value uses long long, is built from LL-suffixed
literals and is printed with %lld. No address or pointer value is printed anywhere.
THE EXECUTION CHARACTER SET IS A SEPARATE IMPLEMENTATION-DEFINED PROPERTY FROM CHAR SIGNEDNESS,
AND IT IS NOT ENGAGED HERE. The paragraph above settles signedness only. C11 5.2.1 leaves the
members of the execution character set and their codes implementation-defined as well, so a
program that printed a character's numeric code, or rendered a literal as bytes, would owe an
accounting of every code it observed. This one owes none: it contains no character constant at
all -- checked mechanically, by stripping comments and string literals and finding zero -- and it
derives no printed VALUE from a character. Its only string literals are printf format strings,
which contribute fixed label text that is byte-identical in all twelve cells of the matrix and in
the golden above. There is therefore no code to pin with a _Static_assert and nothing to narrow.
That is what distinguishes this program from 004_sizeof_alignof.c and
007_string_literal_constants.c in the same area, both of which do print character codes and both
of which pin every code they print for that reason.
NO TARGET IS RESTRICTED AND NO ORACLE IS DISABLED, so the whole matrix is in force for this program:
twelve compile-and-run cells, twelve golden-record assertions, twelve same-target reference
comparisons, and nine cross-backend comparisons against the x86_64 baseline at matching optimization
levels. A divergence in any of them is a compiler defect to be reported as a finding, not an
implementation-defined difference to be excused.
WHAT WOULD LEGITIMATELY BREAK THAT ASSUMPTION, AND HOW IT MUST THEN BE HANDLED: a target on which
sizeof(int), sizeof(unsigned int) or sizeof(long long) differed would still be conforming, so the
resulting difference would be an implementation-defined divergence rather than a compiler defect. It
must in that case be recorded as an expected divergence with this record's target list narrowed and
the reason stated here -- never left to surface as a finding against a backend that did nothing
wrong, and never resolved by dropping the conditional operator's result-type coverage, which is part
of what requirement 2 asks this program to cover.
END
expected_stdout    <<END
